      },
      "id": "RLZ-2BR4MX",
      "invariant": "INV-CK3PTB",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-end-message-belongs-to-its-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Takes the string that names what the tree shows and says the message of every move through `useStatusFor`: the empty message for a move that selected a row, the stop message at a continuation control, the end message at an end.",
      "role": "propagation-persistence"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "049d819910de65c1a893439dc57ab92d95609e5c",
        "content": "sha256:612c3cee6a94e2b191d9d42e6374fdebdfa07b595632f62d8458702779b318bb",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useStatusFor"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-3CW82B",
      "invariant": "INV-CK3PTB",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-end-message-belongs-to-its-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Stores the status together with the rows the committed tree showed when the move was made, and gives it out only while the rows it is called with are those rows. A layout effect drops the stored status in the commit that shows other rows, so it cannot return with the same rows later. Setting the same status for the same rows keeps the state object, and nothing is updated during a render.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "049d819910de65c1a893439dc57ab92d95609e5c",
        "content": "sha256:0eb9bbd2a2cc6669a3c686ffd10d710542006ef5452cb3c9121f678d25711e3b",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "forward"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-W9PW0P",
      "invariant": "INV-MWCCQM",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-kept-partial-family-stop",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Going forward it returns a family's continuation control as the stop when that family has unreturned members, with the family's label for the message, and never a selection: the move only focuses the control. It reads the rendered tree, so a kept family's control is a stop like any other.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    }
  ],
